<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Koxinga</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1624–<a href="/years/1662">1662</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Koxinga, born Zheng Chenggong, was a seventeenth-century Ming loyalist commander who resisted the Qing conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from bases on the south-eastern coast. In 1662 he expelled the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> after besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fort-zeelandia-taiwan">Fort Zeelandia</a>. The loss of Taiwan was a notable setback for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-empire">Dutch Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/koxinga.jpg" alt="Koxinga" width="251" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Portrait_of_Koxinga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
